 "notes": "Cadamuro & Redondo, JCAP 2012 (arXiv:1110.2895). Curve = boundary of the combined cosmological exclusion of Fig. 1 (pics/plot.eps, vector paths extracted; axes calibrated from tick marks: Log10 m 0-11, Log10 g -4 to -18). The union of the paper's own cosmology regions was taken (Optical, EBL, X-rays, x_ion, DM, CMB y/mu, N_eff, D, 4He, EM/Hadr showers), excluding the astrophysical HB and SN regions. Paper's Eq. 1.1 L=-(g/4)F Ftilde phi matches the canonical g_agamma definition, no conversion needed. Trace, ordered by mass: (i) lower-left envelope from ~4.6 eV down to the DM-overclosure edge at m=154 eV (Sec. text: m_phi=154 eV overcloses), where exclusion extends to arbitrarily small g (vertical drop, closed at the figure floor g=1e-18); (ii) along the figure floor to ~2.8e5 eV; (iii) the deuterium spike reaching the figure top (g=1e-4) at m~3e5 eV; (iv) the upper-right envelope (N_eff/4He/Hadr-showers tops) down to (1e11 eV, 6.5e-14). Confidence levels are mixed: N_eff region quoted at 99% CL, 4He at 95% CL; 0.95 reported here. Floor/top values (1e-18, 1e-4) are the figure's axis limits; the true excluded region extends beyond them.",
